From 016046f0b7eb23e3d26b30068da50c8d373bf79d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 05yuki <ceu.azul.samu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:44:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] loading: skip the CPU-only experts in the GPU loader, read
 dense shards ahead

Weight loading for the hybrid MoE. The GPU side's safetensors loader
skips the experts that only the CPU runs, by name, and DeepSeek V4's
`load_weights` skips them too (`KT_LOAD_SKIP_CPU_EXPERTS`); it still
reads the hot lend's experts when `hot-lend` is applied.
`KT_LOAD_PREFETCH=<threads>` reads the dense tensors of each shard ahead
in 16 MiB pieces on a thread pool, so the loaders' mmap faults hit the
page cache. In the kt-kernel wrapper: `KT_GPU_STREAM_DROP_CACHE=<dir>`
drops the page cache of the checkpoint per layer so kt-kernel's arenas
find 2 MB pages; `KT_NUMA_NODES` passes kt-kernel the NUMA nodes to use;
with `--kt-num-gpu-experts 0` the empty GPU weights are not repacked
(dsv41-flash-dual-epyc#2).

Numerics: Bit-identical: the skipped tensors are ones the loader dropped
anyway; the rest is I/O and placement.

Prerequisites: none; applies alone on tier 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C2UBZdnrDZSBh8yQz8rc9g
